{
    "background_story": "Major was a majestic thoroughbred with a storied career in the racing world. Bred from a long line of champions, he was destined for greatness. Under the expert training of his owner, Emma, Major quickly rose through the ranks, winning numerous stakes and accolades. His crowning achievement came when he took the top prize at the prestigious Kentucky Derby, a feat that solidified his reputation as a racing legend. But Major's success wasn't limited to the track. He also excelled as a sire, producing several champion offspring who went on to make their own mark in the racing world. Emma credited Major's success to his intelligence, athleticism, and most importantly, his unbreakable spirit. As he retired to a life of luxury, Major remained a beloved figure in the equestrian community, a symbol of what it means to be a true champion.",
